// aug13l hz1 divergence_000000 (2026-08-14): the first live witness of
// the recursion ruling's documented residual — changed-args-
// same-selection-profile with a const terminal.
//
// RULED (Eric, 2026-08-14): QUIET — the interp is correct. This is an
// OPEN KERNEL OVER-FIRE, not a semantic fork.
//
// f(x-1) over x = iter([0,2,0,4]): every derivation lands on value 8.
// INTERP (1 fire — correct): the outer dispatch's scrutinee changes
// (-1/1/-1/3) but the selection doesn't; the inner call's scrutinee
// fires with the unchanged value 0, its selection is unchanged and its
// arm is const, so the inner select is quiet; the subtraction has no
// fired operand; the arm produces nothing; the select is quiet. One
// emission total (the init derivation). Pure composition of the strict
// select rule + body-driven firing — no recursion-specific machinery.
// KERNEL (4 fires — WRONG): the root call's derivation-changed bit is
// TRUE (root args changed), the damping doesn't reach the
// const-terminal return fold, and the result re-fires 8 per delivery.
//
// THE DECIDING RECEIPT (2026-08-14): the hand-inlined retained twin
// (f calling a distinct g — exact for this input since the inner arg
// is always 0) is QUIET on BOTH engines AND FUSES:
//   {let x = array::iter([i64:0, i64:2, i64:0, i64:4]);
//    let g = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => i64:8};
//    let f = |n: i64| -> i64
//      select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => i64:8 - g(n % i64:1)};
//    f(x - i64:1)}   // AGREE, Trace([1:8]), fused=1
// So the kernel's fire on the recursive form makes recursion
// observable in firing — forbidden by the recursion ruling's headline.
// Same principle as the tail face ruled 2026-08-13 (cceb0809,
// findings/tail-zero-iteration-quiet-aug2026/): production-driven
// firing; the tail-spine control-dependence rationale reaches only
// derivations that actually produce.
//
// THE FIX IS ASPIRE-CLASS: the derivation-changed bit is a root-
// args-changed scalar memo; the exact criterion is "did any production
// reach the result", which needs per-derivation-position selection
// memory the transient-derivation kernel structurally lacks (the
// interp gets it free from retained instances). Rejected cheap fixes:
// root result-value damp is INEXACT (arm body `n % 1 + 8`: the interp
// legitimately fires the unchanged value 8 because the arm produced —
// a value damp flips that case the other way); de-fusing recursive
// callees with result-reachable const terminals catches fib itself
// (`0 => 0, 1 => 1`) and guts recursion fusion coverage.
//
// OUTSIDE the regress corpus (the embedded corpus asserts agreement).
// Soak re-findings of this class are KNOWN — triage as dups.
{let x = array::iter([i64:0, i64:2, i64:0, i64:4]); let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, _ => i64:8 - f(n % i64:1)}; f(x - i64:1)}
